A||||6||fiero56||alarms instead of/along with idiot lights||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||12-31-2000||06:38 PM||||I've been kicking this idea around for quite some time, figured I'd shoot it out here and see what people thought. <BR>I've always thought it would be cool if the oil pressure drops enough to trip the idiot light, or the temp light came on, or any other idiot light were tripped, that a circuit would be closed the blue dinger causing it to sound off a warning that something isn't right. I know most of the lights are right in front of us, but what about us rally guage pod owners, we might miss the oil light, etc. Plus, I'm not always looking down to check my temp, etc. Just something to think about. It seems like a pretty simple addition, and I wouldn't mind doing it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||06:45 PM||||my fiero has the extra gauge cluster for oil and amp. each one has a idiot lite also. you can get those little chimes that can be wired in at auto accesory stores for  less than $10. there a little module about the size of a sugar cube with a few wires. u can add them to headlite or foglites too so u remember to turn them off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-31-2000||09:10 PM||||My chime article tells you all the "logic" of the box and where else to lock at for info. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A><P>Yes you can add lines to be monitored to the existing box but you must know how all the circuits involved are wired and how to use diodes or other items to make sure they aren't cross fed. Otherwise you'll have all the lights on at once.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-31-2000||09:49 PM||||Ogre saves an upcoming day. I would have wired it all up, and been stunned when everything went off at once. Excellent point on the diodes, never would have thought about cross feeding all those lights. Luckily, most of what I learned in those classes I took from college while in high-school are still with me. I remember that capacitors smell like peanut butter when one reverses polarity. Playing with breadboards for hours on end, etc. I think I'll start sometime this week.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-01-2001||11:23 AM||||Another question:<P>What controls the overheat idiot light? Does the ECM control this, or do one of the sensors? Finally, is it possible to adjust what temp the light comes on at?||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-01-2001||01:42 PM||||same sender runs the gauge and light. no it's not adjustable.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kinboyatuwo||01-02-2001||02:09 PM||||I have a custom alarm and for low oil pressure and high temp coolant the alarm continuously chirps<BR>for the redline shifts it chirps once <P>the first two are safety, the last was just to see if we could do it<BR>used an alpine system as the base for the brain and added and played with that<P>really cool!! <P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||4
